from the involution, lower bound because a cycle has length at least 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.card_support_prodSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.card_support_prodSwap","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SignProdComm.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**`d² - d` moved points.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.support_prodSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.support_prodSwap","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SignProdComm.lean#L63-L75","doc":"**The coordinate swap moves exactly the off-diagonal.**\n\nIts fixed points are the pairs `(a, a)`, so the support is `univ.offDiag`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap_sq","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SignProdComm.lean#L58-L61","doc":"**Swapping coordinates twice is the identity.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SignProdComm.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.prodSwap","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SignProdComm.lean#L48-L52","doc":"**The coordinate swap on `ι × ι`, as a permutation.**\n\nDefinitionally `Equiv.prodComm ι ι`; the point of the wrapper is that its declared type has\nhead constant `Equiv.Perm`, so `Equiv.Perm` dot-notation resolves against it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}